IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-employee`
IMPORT `sea-seat-employer`

-- Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 -- worked cases, from the seat of the employer.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2025C00116), never copied from the encoding's output. Every case is HYPOTHETICAL: the
-- shipping company that employs Mia (sea-cases-employee.l4). MIRROR cases ask her facts from this seat; the answers must
-- agree.

§ `cases`

§§ `ss 72, 73, 73A`

-- MIRROR: her incapacity claim received 2 March 2026: decide by 14 March 2026; after the scans asked for on 5 March and
-- received 20 March, by 1 April 2026; the death claim with the 10 to 20 March request, by 10 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I decide the claim` `incapacity for work, property, or the cost of medical treatment (s 73)` (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 14 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I decide the claim` `incapacity for work, property, or the cost of medical treatment (s 73)` (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I decide the claim` `compensation on a death (s 72)` (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 10 5 2026

§§ `s 79`

-- Mia's request for reconsideration received 1 June 2026: reconsider by 31 July 2026. With a request for information on
-- 10 June answered on 15 June, 4 more days (11 to 14 June): 4 August 2026. With an Authority extension to 31 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I reconsider` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 31 7 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I reconsider` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 4 8 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I reconsider` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 31 8 2026) EQUALS Date 31 8 2026

§§ `s 93`

#ASSERT `Am I insured as the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I comply: I am insured or indemnified for my full liability under the Act today (s 93(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I insured as the Act requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am in breach: I must be insured or indemnified for my full liability every day; an offence of strict liability, up to 50 penalty units (s 93(1), (1A))`
-- A policy that covers only some of the crew is not enough.
#ASSERT `Am I insured as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am in breach: I must be insured or indemnified for my full liability every day; an offence of strict liability, up to 50 penalty units (s 93(1), (1A))`

§§ `ss 31, 38, 39`

-- MIRROR: week 51, Mia not working: $1,500. On 19 hours earning $800: $900. The trainee on $400: $360.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay` TRUE 50 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `an amount per week after the first 45 weeks (s 31(4), (5))` 1500
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay` TRUE 50 2000 800 19 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `an amount per week after the first 45 weeks (s 31(4), (5))` 900
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay` TRUE 50 400 100 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `an amount per week after the first 45 weeks (s 31(4), (5))` 360
-- MIRROR: week 11, one of the first 45 weeks.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay` TRUE 10 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `one of the first 45 weeks: compensation by the s 31(2) formula, which is not in the deposited text`
-- MIRROR: a 12% impairment, $12,093.4272; 9%, nothing.
#ASSERT `How much permanent impairment compensation must I pay` FALSE 12 100778.56 EQUALS 12093.4272
#ASSERT `How much permanent impairment compensation must I pay` FALSE 9 100778.56 EQUALS 0
